   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener>
               Columbia University<lb/>
               in the City of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs><lb/>THE REVIEW OF RELIGION<lb/>
               <dateline>401 Low Memorial Library<lb/> <date when="1940-05-15">May 15, 1940</date></dateline>
               <salute>My dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>We must call your attention to the fact that your review of <rs
                  rend="#tillich_person_id__1783" type="person">Siegfried</rs>&apos;s <rs
                  type="bibls">Das Protestantische Prinzip in Kirche und Welt</rs> is long overdue.
               It is a 1939 publication, and we do not like to have our reviews grow stale,– also
               the publishers do not like it! Unfortunately the next issue of the REVIEW does not
               appear until fall, but I must urge you to let us have the review before August
               without fail.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4051" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Marguerite Block</hi><lb/>Secretary</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
